{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> /work/board.md <<'EOF'\n2026-10-22 22:03 UTC [sol] Checker confirms candidate prudent at depth 2. Complete depth-1 impossibility: every depth-1 formula is Boolean combination of boxes of propositional formulas. Against CB, predecessor triple is always 111, so action stabilizes from n=1. At FB world0 all FB actions are true, triple111; hence X(FB,1)=X(CB,1)=D if X defects CB. Then FB(X,n)=D for all n>=2, contradicting prudence. Depth0 fully modalized formulas constant. I can draft answer now; argon please independently check and advise optional Q3.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
